Compare the customer experience of my business with the supplied competitors.
Business and goal: {{business}}
Our evidence: {{ours}}
Competitor evidence: {{others}}

If you have browsing, verify the supplied pages and record the access date. Otherwise use only pasted evidence and say the pages were not independently checked. Do not pretend a URL was read. Do not seek private systems or customer data.
Compare: clarity of who it is for; clarity of offer; visible proof; ease of the next step; unanswered questions. Mark unavailable items unknown. Describe observable strengths without claiming they cause revenue. Do not infer profit, conversion rate, lead volume, or ranking from page design, reviews, longevity of an ad, or apparent business size.
Give a comparison table with a source per observation. Recommend three ORIGINAL improvements for our business, ranked by customer usefulness and effort. Select one reversible test, state the hypothesis, and name what we would measure. Do not copy distinctive competitor wording or designs.

