Help me choose one small AI experiment.
My business: {{business}}
My last busy day: {{week}}
What should stay human: {{limits}}

If my answer is vague or “not sure,” interview me one question at a time. Begin with “What did you have to type or explain more than once yesterday?” Ask no more than four questions before proposing a first experiment.
Look for repeated work with clear inputs, a reviewable output, and a simple way to know if it is right. Rank at most three tasks by frequency, effort, cost of a mistake, and ease of checking. Use unknown when facts are missing. Do not recommend products or subscriptions yet.
Choose one low-risk task to try on a synthetic or anonymized example. Give its input, expected output, what I check, a stop condition, and a 15-minute first step. Name one task I should leave alone for now. Track drafting time plus review time against the manual approach. Potential savings are a hypothesis, not a promise.

