Improve a homepage by starting with the customer.
Current text: {{current}}
Customer evidence and proof: {{customers}}
Offer and next action: {{offer}}

First summarize the customer's immediate question and what the supplied evidence supports. Mark inferences. If I provide only a URL and you cannot browse it, ask me for the text instead of pretending to have read it.
Explain the three biggest clarity problems in the current text. Then draft: one headline, one supporting sentence, one button label, three concise reasons to continue, and one answer to the most important unanswered question. Prefer specifics to adjectives. Keep any unavailable proof marked [PROOF NEEDED] outside the publishable copy.
Show why each change helps a customer decide. Do not invent reviews, credentials, certifications, prices, service areas, response times, guarantees, or performance gains. End with the exact facts I need to verify before publishing.

