Turn my software idea into a small, testable build brief.
Idea: {{idea}}
Current process: {{process}}
Limits and existing tools: {{limits}}

Identify the user, their job, and the smallest useful outcome. Ask up to three essential questions if those are missing; do not design a large system around guesses.
Produce: one-sentence purpose; one main user journey; minimum inputs and outputs; explicit exclusions; data access and retention needs; one normal example; one error case; and five observable acceptance checks. Compare a simple manual or existing-tool version with a new build. Recommend the simplest route that meets the stated need without claiming you checked a product you did not inspect.
Separate choices we can make now from unknowns a builder must verify. Do not invent integration access, security guarantees, development cost, timeline, or legal compliance. This is a brief, not completed software.

